WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.510 align:start position:0%
 
this is tamar hussein reading for  reviewer steven petty when mario golf  super rush is at its best  chaos is what makes it tick its many  unpredictable moments are delightfully  humorous  adding a new dimension to camelot's  long-running sports series  zany courses designed to look more like  3d super mario levels  and a pair of new fast-paced modes turn  the typically leisurely sport of golf  into an action game  super rush tries to add to its variety  even in its pair of control schemes  a button based swing system and motion  controls the button based control scheme  differs slightly from previous entries  this time around you click once to start  your swing accuracy is determined by  shift  marks outside of the meter that funnel  outward off the tee and in the fairway  the marks are confined to the top but  when you have a bad lie  they start much lower making it less  likely to hit your shots on target  super rush's button based swing system  rewards finding the short grass  motion controls on the other hand hark  back to the simplicity of wii sports  unfortunately this doesn't really work  when playing super rush's tricky courses  four swings are manageable  but any shot that requires a delicate  swing is too much of a guessing game  it was immediately clear that motion  controls were simply incompatible with  the elaborate designs  camelot created to highlight the new  leading game mode of  golf that said mastering the three click  swing system including shaping the golf  ball  adding backspin and tinkering with  trajectories is more important than ever  because the courses are littered with  obstacles which also make you think more  about the type of shot you want to hit  in speed golf you're racing to finish  each hole as fast as you can  each shot adds 30 seconds to your time  so you need to try to play well  while maintaining a brisk pace  speedgolf adds a new layer of strategy  and chaos since everyone plays  simultaneously  an unfortunate downside to speedgolf is  that you can never admire your good  shots  because you're running down the fairway  towards your ball battle golf uses the  mechanics of speed golfs and cranks up  the mayhem  it pits up to four players against each  other in a stadium course with nine  flags to aim at  the first player to secure three flags  wins the twist here  is that once a flag is claimed it's gone  from the game battle golf emphasizes  both skill  and strategy there are two layouts  available one that's fairly  straightforward and another that's  littered with enemies obstacles and  hazards  due to its design battlegolf conjures up  even more random chaos than speed golf  making it an optimal party game with  lightning quick rounds that never have a  dull moment  each of the 16 playable characters are  equipped with a pair of moves that can  be deployed strategically in these  fast-paced modes special shot and super  dash for instance  wario's special shot creates lightning  strikes that toy with your shots  yoshi rolls around on a giant egg when  dashing while charging chuck looks like  a fullback trying to mow down the  competition  each golfer's unique super dash can help  them to get to the ball faster  but it also can be a deterrent for  competitors progress since you can knock  opponents down while running  meanwhile a well timed and placed  special shot can knock other golfers  balls from a good position to a not  ideal spot  these two central mechanics often look  cool in motion and are incredibly useful  in speed golf  it's clear why speedgolf rules mario  golf super rush when you step onto the  links  with the exception of two traditional  courses that look like golf courses  you'd find in real life  super rush's courses teeter between  absurd and diabolical  and i say this as a compliment ridge  rock lake is set along cliffs surrounded  by water and features broiders rolling  across fairways  typhus guarding greens and wind tunnels  that can send you and your ball up to  another level there's a lot of fun  strategy involved here thanks to the  elevation changes  and the scattered layout  [Music]  balmy dunes a desert themed course with  towering pokies  giant sand mars surrounding the fairways  quicksand and elevation changes galore  is a sprawling track that works  wonderfully for speed golf  because of the enemy placement barmy  dunes often forces you to get creative  with shots  hitting fades around pokies and high  launching shots over those pesky sand  mars  another course wild weather woods uses  unpredictable conditions to mess with  your game randomized spots on the course  are prone to lightning strikes if you  swing your club too far back  costing you a stroke and precious time  meanwhile biddy buds waddle across the  fairway and piranha creepers poke their  chompy heads out  requiring you to zigzag to your ball the  final course bowser highlands  is a molten themed track with lava  bubbles emerging from the fiery depth  magmas creeping over the edge of danger  bombs whomps and chain chomps scattered  across the fairways  and fireballs circling platforms you  need to cross it's the most perilous  course of the bunch due to the sheer  number of hazards and obstacles  making for a fitting swan song  nice shot  even though super rush features some of  the best courses in series history  it's a tad underwhelming to only have  six at release especially since two of  them  though great for traditional golf  purists feel like standard mario golf  fare  though nintendo has vowed to release  free post launch content for super rush  world tour for 3ds had 10 courses at  launch to unlock all of the clever and  playful courses  you have to work your way through golfer  adventure as your me as the tempo  game mode golf adventure isn't the fully  fledged role-playing golf journey it  seems to be from the outset  it offers very little besides a primer  to what super rush is all about  despite the semi-open world layout with  hubs for each course and  npc scattered throughout super rush's  world feels shallow  with nothing to do besides the next main  line event golfer adventure doesn't even  allow you to use motion controls  probably because you'd have a hard time  reaching credits as a rookie working  towards becoming a golf superstar you  earn badges that unlock new tournaments  and courses  what's particularly strange about golf  adventures challenges is that you only  ever play a full  18 hole round one time it's often  segmented into smaller challenges  where you have to shoot better than a  certain score or under time restraints  and almost the entire roughly six hour  campaign center is on speed golf  you only play short spurts of  traditional golf and never in a  tournament  round like mario tennis aces there are a  few boss battles each of which utilize  the mechanics in fun ways  even if they are short-lived duels the  lackluster golf adventure does have a  few standout challenges at least  ridge rock lake's cross country golf  event tasks you with completing nine  holes in under 40 strokes but you get to  choose which order to complete the holes  in which adds some welcome strategy to  the breezy mode  bowser highlands is also markedly  different in golf adventure  as it mixes fire and ice holes the snowy  holes feature ice bros  sliding freezies and other super mario  staples the mix between fire and ice  makes bowser highlands feel like two  courses sandwiched into one which winds  up making a really interesting course  that sadly can't be played outside of  golf adventure  unfortunately ai controlled golfers are  absolutely horrendous in golf adventure  not just in the beginning but all  throughout the campaign this presents an  issue since speedgolf requires you to  wait for your opponents to finish the  hole before moving on to the next  watching pink yoshi turn away from the  flag stick and chunk yet another shot  into the rough after you're already done  gross tiresome  and watching insert any character name  actively aim away from the hole on a  perfectly straight puck can become  infuriating  the biggest blunder of golf adventure is  that once the credit rolls there's  nothing really left to do  you can go back and level up your  character and round out your set of golf  clubs  but it's not even possible to replay  certain sections of the game golfer  adventure doesn't even track any of your  best scores so there isn't  any real reason to do so anyway there is  a separate solo challenge mode that  keeps track of your best scores  but it seems like a weird decision to  not roll this into an end game for golf  adventure  like many sports games mario golf super  rush's legs come from multiplayer  against real humans  whether they be online or locally when  playing locally up to four golfers can  jump into standard golf but only two can  play at a time in battle golf and speed  golf  it should be noted that ai golfers play  markedly better outside of golf  adventure which makes playing a round of  speed golf against the computer much  more fun than in golf adventure  with three radically different styles of  play and some seriously inventive  courses  mario golf super rush is a compellingly  original sports game  speed golf and battle golf actively make  you adapt to wild different conditions  while balancing technique and speediness  the three click swing system still feels  great  though if you desire an accurate motion  controlled golf game this isn't it  golfer adventure curiously lacks a  conventional tournament structure  or record keeping making it a tough sell  to revisit  super rush isn't the best entry in the  series  but it is a worthy addition  [Music]  nice  [Music]

